# Self-Supervised Segmentation of Synaptic Structures in Fluorescence Microscopy

> Bachelor's thesis — self-supervised pretraining (SimMIM + VICReg) of a Swin Transformer encoder on 3-channel confocal fluorescence microscopy, followed by downstream segmentation of synaptic puncta.

---

## Overview

This repository implements a full pipeline for synaptic structure analysis in fluorescence microscopy images:

```
Raw microscopy  ➜  Patch extraction  ➜  SSL pretraining  ➜  Downstream segmentation
     (.czi/.ets/.vsi)    (128×128 / 32×32)    (SimMIM + VICReg)     (SwinUNETR)
```

The encoder is a **MONAI Swin-Tiny** backbone pretrained with a combination of **SimMIM** (masked image modeling) and **VICReg** (variance-invariance-covariance regularization), optionally initialized from **MoBY** contrastive weights. The pretrained encoder is then fine-tuned for pixel-level segmentation of pre-synaptic and post-synaptic puncta.

---

